# Market integrations

The Market lets admins browse online catalogs and add books to the library. Each catalog type is an **integration**: a small module that fetches the catalog and maps it into Bookserve's types. Bookserve owns everything else: the store UI, caching, validation, downloading, EPUB checks, provenance and metadata.

An admin adds **sources** in Settings → Market sources. A source is an integration plus its settings (for example, an OPDS catalog URL and credentials), with its own id. Books added from a source are linked to it in `book_sources`.

Built-in integrations:

- `gutenberg`: Project Gutenberg (`src/lib/market/integrations/gutenberg.ts`). Seeded as the default source.
- `opds`: any OPDS 1.x catalog (`src/lib/market/integrations/opds.ts`).

## Goals

- **One Market, many stores.** Users see a single store: one search, one home, one book dialog. Each source's books appear in it as the same cards, merged with copies from other sources. A new store adds books to the Market; it does not add a new page or feature.
- **All store-specific code lives in its integration.** Quirks of a catalog (odd feeds, auth, id formats, missing fields) are handled there, so the rest of Bookserve never knows which store a book came from.
- **Anyone can write one.** The contract in `sdk.ts` is small and stable enough that a third party can write an integration without reading the rest of the codebase. Integrations will later be loadable from `<data>/plugins/`, so the built-in ones must follow the same rules.

## Where code goes

| Code                                                                                | Lives in                                                            |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Talking to a store: fetching, parsing, auth, mapping to `BookSummary`/`BookDetails` | `src/lib/market/integrations/<id>.ts`                               |
| The contract and helpers integrations may use                                       | `src/lib/market/sdk.ts`                                             |
| Running integrations: context, cache, timeouts, cleaning their output               | `src/lib/market/host.ts`                                            |
| Merging sources: deduplication, rows, shelves                                       | `src/lib/market/merge.ts`                                           |
| Server functions: sources, browsing, adding to the library                          | `src/lib/market-functions.ts`                                       |
| UI                                                                                  | `src/routes/_app/market.tsx`, `src/routes/_app/settings/market.tsx` |

Never:

- Check which integration or source something came from outside its integration (no `if (integration.id === 'gutenberg')` in the host, server functions, merge code or UI).
- Add a store-specific route, server function, table, setting screen or UI branch.
- Import Bookserve modules other than `#/lib/market/sdk` from an integration, or use `fetch`, the database or the filesystem directly.

When an integration needs something the contract lacks (a field, a capability, a kind of setting), extend `sdk.ts` for every integration: an optional field or method that the host and UI handle generically. If an existing integration would break, bump `apiVersion`. If the store speaks standard OPDS, use the `opds` integration instead of writing a new one; write a bespoke one only when its catalog needs smoothing over, as Gutenberg's does.

## Writing an integration

An integration is a `MarketIntegration` object from `src/lib/market/sdk.ts`. Import only from that module: it also exports the helpers integrations need (`parseFeed`, `parseOpenSearch`, `fillSearchTemplate` and `resolveUrl` for OPDS feeds, `htmlToText`).

```ts
import { defineIntegration } from '#/lib/market/sdk'

export const example = defineIntegration({
  id: 'example', // stored on sources and book_sources; never change it
  name: 'Example Books',
  apiVersion: 1,
  // Fields the admin fills in when adding a source; read them from ctx.settings.
  settings: [
    { key: 'apiKey', label: 'API key', type: 'password', required: true },
  ],

  // Optional: called when a source is added. Throw to reject the settings.
  async check(ctx) {
    await ctx.fetch('https://example.com/api/me', { headers: auth(ctx) })
  },

  // The landing page: rows of books, and shelves (categories) to browse.
  async home(ctx) {
    return {
      // `kind` ('popular' or 'new') merges the row with other sources' rows
      // of that kind; rows without one merge by title.
      rows: [
        {
          id: 'popular',
          kind: 'popular',
          title: 'Popular',
          description: null,
          books: [],
        },
      ],
      shelves: [{ id: 'fiction', title: 'Fiction', description: null }],
    }
  },

  // A shelf, row or any id you returned in a ShelfLink; `cursor` is the
  // nextCursor you returned for the previous page.
  async shelf(ctx, shelfId, cursor) {
    return { title: 'Fiction', shelves: [], books: [], nextCursor: null }
  },

  // Optional; without it there is no search box.
  async search(ctx, query, cursor) {
    return { title: query, shelves: [], books: [], nextCursor: null }
  },

  async book(ctx, bookId) {
    return {
      id: bookId,
      title: '…',
      authors: ['…'],
      coverUrl: null,
      description: null,
      language: 'en',
      publisher: null,
      publishedDate: null,
      isbn: null,
      subjects: [],
      shelves: [], // related shelves: the author, series, categories
      formats: [{ id: 'epub', label: 'EPUB', size: null }], // EPUB only, best first
    }
  },

  // The EPUB file. Bookserve streams the body into the library; ctx.fetch
  // gets a longer timeout here.
  async download(ctx, bookId, formatId) {
    return ctx.fetch(`https://example.com/books/${bookId}.epub`, {
      headers: auth(ctx),
    })
  },
})
```

Then register it in `INTEGRATIONS` in `src/lib/market/host.ts`. It shows up in the "Add source" dialog, with a form built from `settings`.

The Market shows every source at once, merging the same book from different sources into one entry, and home rows or shelves with the same title into one. Books merge on ISBN, or on title (up to any `:`, `;`, `(`, `[`, `-` or `--`) plus the first author's surname, never across languages. Set `isbn` and `language` on a `BookSummary` when the catalog has them.

## Rules

- **Ids are yours.** Book, shelf, format ids and cursors are opaque strings that Bookserve passes back unchanged. Book ids must be stable: they are stored in `book_sources.external_id` to show "In library" and to avoid adding a book twice. They arrive from the browser, so validate them before building URLs (see `catalogPath` in the Gutenberg integration).
- **Use `ctx.fetch`**, not `fetch`: it takes `method`, `headers`, `body` and `timeoutMs`, allows only http(s) URLs, adds a timeout and Bookserve's User-Agent, and throws on network errors and non-2xx responses with a message the UI shows as is. Throw an `Error` with a short message for anything else ("Unknown book").
- **Use `ctx.cached(key, ttlMs, load)`** for anything `book()` and `download()` refetch. Its cache is per source and in memory.
- **Return plain data.** Text is plain (no HTML; the SDK's `htmlToText` converts). Dates are `YYYY`, `YYYY-MM` or `YYYY-MM-DD`. Cover URLs are http(s). Bookserve trims and drops anything malformed (`src/lib/market/host.ts`), so a buggy integration can't break the page.
- **EPUB only.** List only EPUB formats; return an empty `formats` list for books without one. The download is checked to be a valid EPUB before it is added.
- **Don't fill in metadata you don't have.** When a book is added, its EPUB's own metadata wins; the integration's description, language, publisher, date, ISBN and cover only fill gaps (stored as a match in `books.matched`, so "Revert to file metadata" removes them).
- **Trust.** Integrations run in the server process with full access, so only add code you trust. Settings of type `password` are never sent to the browser.
- **Versioning.** `apiVersion` is `1`. A breaking change to the SDK bumps it, and integrations with another version are not loaded.
=== FILES ===
src/lib/market:
AGENTS.md
host.ts
integrations
merge.ts
opds.ts
sdk.ts

src/lib/market/integrations:
gutenberg.ts
opds.ts

# Market

The Market is built on pluggable integrations. Read `docs/market-integrations.md` before changing anything here or adding a store.

- Adding a store means adding an integration in `integrations/<id>.ts` that implements `MarketIntegration` from `sdk.ts`, registered in `INTEGRATIONS` in `host.ts`. Nothing else should change.
- Integrations import only from `#/lib/market/sdk` and fetch only through `ctx.fetch`.
- Store-specific code lives only in its integration. Never branch on an integration or source id in `host.ts`, `merge.ts`, `src/lib/market-functions.ts` or the Market UI.
- If an integration needs something the contract lacks, extend `sdk.ts` generically (an optional field or method the host and UI handle for every source), update the docs, and bump `apiVersion` if it breaks existing integrations.
=== SDK ===
// The contract for Market integrations. An integration fetches a store's
// catalog and maps it into these types; Bookserve owns everything else (the
// UI, caching, validation, downloading, EPUB checks and the library). See
// docs/market-integrations.md.

export const MARKET_API_VERSION = 1

export type BookSummary = {
  // Stable id within the integration; passed back to book() and download().
  id: string
  title: string
  authors: string[]
  coverUrl: string | null
  // When known in lists, these help the Market merge copies of a book from
  // different sources (it also merges by title and author).
  isbn?: string | null
  // ISO 639 code, e.g. `en`; copies in different languages never merge.
  language?: string | null
}

export type Format = {
  // Passed back to download().
  id: string
  // e.g. "EPUB3 (with images)".
  label: string
  // Bytes, when known.
  size: number | null
}

export type BookDetails = BookSummary & {
  // Plain text; blank lines separate paragraphs.
  description: string | null
  publisher: string | null
  // `YYYY`, `YYYY-MM` or `YYYY-MM-DD`.
  publishedDate: string | null
  subjects: string[]
  // Related shelves: more by the author, the same series or category...
  shelves: ShelfLink[]
  // EPUB downloads only, best first. Empty when the book has no EPUB.
  formats: Format[]
}

// A list to browse into: a category, author, subject, search refinement...
export type ShelfLink = {
  // Passed back to shelf().
  id: string
  title: string
  description: string | null
}

export type Listing = {
  title: string
  shelves: ShelfLink[]
  books: BookSummary[]
  // Pass back to get the next page; null on the last page.
  nextCursor: string | null
}

// What a home row is, so rows from different sources merge even when their
// titles differ. Rows without a kind merge by title.
export type RowKind = 'popular' | 'new'

// The landing page: rows of books, plus shelves to browse.
export type Home = {
  rows: Array<ShelfLink & { kind?: RowKind; books: BookSummary[] }>
  shelves: ShelfLink[]
}

export type SettingField = {
  key: string
  label: string
  type: 'text' | 'url' | 'password'
  required?: boolean
  placeholder?: string
}

export type IntegrationContext = {
  // The source's settings, as entered by an admin (keys from `settings`).
  settings: Record<string, string>
  // fetch for http(s) URLs, with a timeout and Bookserve's User-Agent. Throws
  // on network errors ("Timed out", "Could not connect") and on non-2xx
  // responses. The timeout covers reading the body; downloads get a longer one.
  fetch: (url: string, init?: FetchInit) => Promise<Response>
  // Memoizes `load` under `key` for `ttlMs`, per source. Failures aren't cached.
  cached: <T>(key: string, ttlMs: number, load: () => Promise<T>) => Promise<T>
}

export type FetchInit = {
  method?: string
  headers?: Record<string, string>
  body?: string | URLSearchParams
  timeoutMs?: number
}

export type MarketIntegration = {
  id: string
  name: string
  apiVersion: typeof MARKET_API_VERSION
  // Admin-entered settings per source (server URL, credentials...).
  settings: SettingField[]
  // Called when a source is added; throw to reject its settings.
  check?: (ctx: IntegrationContext) => Promise<void>
  home: (ctx: IntegrationContext) => Promise<Home>
  shelf: (
    ctx: IntegrationContext,
    shelfId: string,
    cursor: string | null,
  ) => Promise<Listing>
  // Optional: no search box without it.
  search?: (
    ctx: IntegrationContext,
    query: string,
    cursor: string | null,
  ) => Promise<Listing>
  book: (ctx: IntegrationContext, bookId: string) => Promise<BookDetails>
  // The EPUB file, usually `return ctx.fetch(url)`; Bookserve streams the
  // body into the library.
  download: (
    ctx: IntegrationContext,
    bookId: string,
    formatId: string,
  ) => Promise<Response>
}

// Helpers for integrations. Import everything from this module only.
export { htmlToText } from '#/lib/epub'
export {
  fillSearchTemplate,
  parseFeed,
  parseOpenSearch,
  resolveUrl,
} from '#/lib/market/opds'
export type { OpdsDownload, OpdsEntry, OpdsFeed } from '#/lib/market/opds'

export function defineIntegration(integration: MarketIntegration) {
  return integration
}
=== HOST ===
import { HttpError, request } from '#/lib/metadata/http'
import { gutenberg } from '#/lib/market/integrations/gutenberg'
import { opds } from '#/lib/market/integrations/opds'
import { MARKET_API_VERSION } from '#/lib/market/sdk'
import type {
  BookDetails,
  BookSummary,
  Home,
  IntegrationContext,
  Listing,
  MarketIntegration,
  RowKind,
  ShelfLink,
} from '#/lib/market/sdk'

// Runs integrations for the Market: builds their context, and checks and
// trims everything they return before it reaches the UI or the library.

// Built-in integrations. Add new ones here.
export const INTEGRATIONS: Record<string, MarketIntegration> =
  Object.fromEntries(
    [gutenberg, opds]
      .filter((i) => i.apiVersion === MARKET_API_VERSION)
      .map((i) => [i.id, i]),
  )

export function getIntegration(id: string) {
  const integration = INTEGRATIONS[id]
  if (!integration) throw new Error(`Unknown integration: ${id}`)
  return integration
}

const TIMEOUT_MS = 15_000
export const DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS = 10 * 60_000
const MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES = 200

// Per source; module state, so it lasts as long as the process.
const caches = new Map<
  string,
  Map<string, { at: number; value: Promise<unknown> }>
>()

// `timeoutMs` is the default for ctx.fetch: DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS for download().
export function createContext(
  cacheKey: string,
  settings: Record<string, string>,
  timeoutMs = TIMEOUT_MS,
): IntegrationContext {
  let cache = caches.get(cacheKey)
  if (!cache) caches.set(cacheKey, (cache = new Map()))
  const entries = cache
  return {
    settings,
    async fetch(url, init) {
      if (!/^https?:\/\//i.test(url)) throw new Error('Invalid URL')
      const res = await request(url, init?.timeoutMs ?? timeoutMs, init)
      if (!res.ok) throw new HttpError(res.status)
      return res
    },
    cached<T>(key: string, ttlMs: number, load: () => Promise<T>) {
      const hit = entries.get(key)
      if (hit && Date.now() - hit.at < ttlMs) return hit.value as Promise<T>
      const value = load()
      entries.set(key, { at: Date.now(), value })
      value.catch(() => entries.delete(key))
      // Drop the oldest entries; Maps iterate in insertion order.
      for (const k of entries.keys()) {
        if (entries.size <= MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES) break
        entries.delete(k)
      }
      return value
    },
  }
}

export function clearCache(cacheKey: string) {
  caches.delete(cacheKey)
}

const ROW_KINDS: RowKind[] = ['popular', 'new']

const str = (value: unknown, max = 500) =>
  typeof value === 'string' ? value.trim().slice(0, max) : ''

const strs = (value: unknown, max = 50) =>
  Array.isArray(value)
    ? value
        .map((v) => str(v))
        .filter(Boolean)
        .slice(0, max)
    : []

const httpUrl = (value: unknown) => {
  const url = str(value, 2000)
  return /^https?:\/\//i.test(url) ? url : null
}

const size = (value: unknown) =>
  Number.isSafeInteger(value) && (value as number) > 0
    ? (value as number)
    : null

function summary(book: BookSummary): BookSummary {
  return {
    id: str(book.id, 2000),
    title: str(book.title) || 'Untitled',
    authors: strs(book.authors),
    coverUrl: httpUrl(book.coverUrl),
    isbn: str(book.isbn, 20).replace(/[^\dX]/gi, '') || null,
    language: str(book.language, 20) || null,
  }
}

function shelf(link: ShelfLink): ShelfLink {
  return {
    id: str(link.id, 2000),
    title: str(link.title) || 'Untitled',
    description: str(link.description, 1000) || null,
  }
}

const books = (list: BookSummary[]) =>
  (Array.isArray(list) ? list : []).map(summary).filter((b) => b.id)
const shelves = (list: ShelfLink[]) =>
  (Array.isArray(list) ? list : []).map(shelf).filter((s) => s.id)

export function cleanHome(home: Home): Home {
  return {
    rows: (Array.isArray(home.rows) ? home.rows : [])
      .map((row) => ({
        ...shelf(row),
        kind: ROW_KINDS.includes(row.kind!) ? row.kind : undefined,
        books: books(row.books),
      }))
      .filter((row) => row.id && row.books.length),
    shelves: shelves(home.shelves),
  }
}

export function cleanListing(listing: Listing): Listing {
  return {
    title: str(listing.title) || 'Untitled',
    shelves: shelves(listing.shelves),
    books: books(listing.books),
    nextCursor: str(listing.nextCursor, 2000) || null,
  }
}

export function cleanDetails(book: BookDetails): BookDetails {
  const date = str(book.publishedDate)
  return {
    ...summary(book),
    description: str(book.description, 20_000) || null,
    publisher: str(book.publisher) || null,
    publishedDate: /^\d{4}(-\d{2}(-\d{2})?)?$/.test(date) ? date : null,
    subjects: strs(book.subjects),
    shelves: shelves(book.shelves),
    formats: (Array.isArray(book.formats) ? book.formats : [])
      .map((f) => ({
        id: str(f.id, 2000),
        label: str(f.label) || 'EPUB',
        size: size(f.size),
      }))
      .filter((f) => f.id),
  }
}

import { defineIntegration, parseFeed } from '#/lib/market/sdk'
import type {
  BookSummary,
  IntegrationContext,
  Listing,
  OpdsEntry,
  ShelfLink,
} from '#/lib/market/sdk'

// Project Gutenberg, through its OPDS catalog, with its quirks smoothed over:
// lists link to a feed per book, so covers come from Gutenberg's predictable
// cover URLs; a book's feed has one entry per build (with and without images),
// merged into one book; descriptions come from the "Summary:" field.

const BASE = 'https://www.gutenberg.org'
const CACHE_MS = 10 * 60_000

const ROWS = [
  {
    id: 'popular',
    kind: 'popular' as const,
    title: 'Popular',
    path: '/ebooks/search.opds/?sort_order=downloads',
  },
  {
    id: 'latest',
    kind: 'new' as const,
    title: 'Latest',
    path: '/ebooks/search.opds/?sort_order=release_date',
  },
]

// Gutenberg's "Category:" bookshelves.
const CATEGORIES: Array<[number, string]> = [
  [645, 'Novels'],
  [649, 'Classics of Literature'],
  [644, 'Adventure'],
  [638, 'Science Fiction & Fantasy'],
  [640, 'Crime, Thrillers & Mystery'],
  [639, 'Romance'],
  [635, 'Historical Novels'],
  [634, 'Short Stories'],
  [637, 'Poetry'],
  [642, 'Plays, Films & Dramas'],
  [641, 'Humour'],
  [636, 'Children & Young Adult'],
  [646, 'Mythology & Folklore'],
  [643, 'Biographies'],
  [647, 'Essays, Letters & Speeches'],
  [648, 'Travel Writing'],
]

// Labels for Gutenberg's EPUB builds (keyed by the download URL's suffix).
const FORMAT_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
  'epub3.images': 'EPUB 3',
  'epub.images': 'EPUB 2 (older e-readers)',
  'epub.noimages': 'EPUB 2 without images',
}

const formatRank = (id: string) => {
  const rank = Object.keys(FORMAT_LABELS).indexOf(id)
  return rank < 0 ? 99 : rank
}

const coverUrl = (id: string) =>
  `${BASE}/cache/epub/${id}/pg${id}.cover.medium.jpg`

const displayName = (name: string) =>
  name.replace(/^([^,]+), ([^,]+)$/, '$2 $1')

// "Books in Category: Romance", "By Austen, Jane…" → "Romance", "Jane Austen".
function shelfTitle(title: string) {
  const t = title
    .replace(/…$/, '')
    .replace(/^Books /, '')
    .replace(/^(in|on) (Category: )?/i, '')
  return /^by /i.test(t) ? displayName(t.slice(3)) : t
}

// A catalog path on gutenberg.org from a shelf id, cursor or href. Author and
// subject searches are blocked for bots, so they aren't shelves.
function catalogPath(value: string) {
  const url = new URL(value, BASE)
  if (
    url.origin !== BASE ||
    !url.pathname.startsWith('/ebooks/') ||
    /^\/ebooks\/\w+\/search/.test(url.pathname)
  ) {
    return null
  }
  return url.pathname + url.search
}

function feed(ctx: IntegrationContext, path: string) {
  return ctx.cached(path, CACHE_MS, async () => {
    const res = await ctx.fetch(BASE + path)
    return parseFeed(await res.text(), BASE + path)
  })
}

async function listing(
  ctx: IntegrationContext,
  path: string | null,
  title?: string,
): Promise<Listing> {
  if (!path) throw new Error('Unknown shelf')
  const f = await feed(ctx, path)
  const books: BookSummary[] = []
  const shelves: ShelfLink[] = []
  for (const entry of f.entries) {
    const id = entry.href?.match(
      /^https:\/\/www\.gutenberg\.org\/ebooks\/(\d+)\.opds$/,
    )?.[1]
    const shelf = entry.href ? catalogPath(entry.href) : null
    if (id) {
      // In lists, the content is the author, or a download count without one.
      const author = entry.summary && !/^\d+ downloads$/.test(entry.summary)
      books.push({
        id,
        title: entry.title,
        authors: author ? [entry.summary!] : [],
        coverUrl: coverUrl(id),
      })
    } else if (shelf) {
      shelves.push({
        id: shelf,
        title: shelfTitle(entry.title),
        description: entry.summary,
      })
    }
  }
  return {
    title: title ?? shelfTitle(f.title),
    shelves,
    books,
    nextCursor: f.next ? catalogPath(f.next) : null,
  }
}

// The builds in a book's feed, largest first (the one with images).
async function builds(ctx: IntegrationContext, id: string) {
  if (!/^\d+$/.test(id)) throw new Error('Unknown book')
  const { entries } = await feed(ctx, `/ebooks/${id}.opds`)
  if (!entries.length) throw new Error('Unknown book')
  const largest = (e: OpdsEntry) =>
    Math.max(0, ...e.downloads.map((d) => d.size ?? 0))
  return [...entries].sort((a, b) => largest(b) - largest(a))
}

// "epub3.images" from https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1342.epub3.images.
function formatId(id: string, href: string) {
  const prefix = `${BASE}/ebooks/${id}.`
  return href.startsWith(prefix) ? href.slice(prefix.length) : null
}

export const gutenberg = defineIntegration({
  id: 'gutenberg',
  name: 'Project Gutenberg',
  apiVersion: 1,
  settings: [],

  async home(ctx) {
    const rows = await Promise.all(
      ROWS.map(async (row) => ({
        id: row.id,
        kind: row.kind,
        title: row.title,
        description: null,
        books: (await listing(ctx, row.path)).books,
      })),
    )
    return {
      rows,
      shelves: CATEGORIES.map(([id, title]) => ({
        id: `/ebooks/bookshelf/${id}.opds?sort_order=downloads`,
        title,
        description: null,
      })),
    }
  },

  shelf(ctx, shelfId, cursor) {
    const row = ROWS.find((r) => r.id === shelfId)
    const category = CATEGORIES.find(
      ([id]) => shelfId === `/ebooks/bookshelf/${id}.opds?sort_order=downloads`,
    )
    return listing(
      ctx,
      catalogPath(cursor ?? row?.path ?? shelfId),
      row?.title ?? category?.[1],
    )
  },

  async search(ctx, query, cursor) {
    const result = await listing(
      ctx,
      cursor
        ? catalogPath(cursor)
        : `/ebooks/search.opds/?query=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,
    )
    return { ...result, title: query }
  },

  async book(ctx, id) {
    const entries = await builds(ctx, id)
    const main = entries[0]
    const summary = main.summary?.match(
      /(?:^|\n)Summary:\s*([\s\S]*?)(?:\n\s*\n|$)/,
    )?.[1]
    const formats = entries
      .flatMap((e) => e.downloads)
      .flatMap((d) => {
        const fid = formatId(id, d.href)
        return fid
          ? [{ id: fid, label: FORMAT_LABELS[fid] ?? d.title, size: d.size }]
          : []
      })
      .sort((a, b) => formatRank(a.id) - formatRank(b.id))
    return {
      id,
      title: main.title,
      authors: main.authors,
      coverUrl: main.coverUrl ?? coverUrl(id),
      description: summary?.trim() || null,
      language: main.language,
      // Gutenberg's dates are its own release dates, not publication dates.
      publisher: null,
      publishedDate: null,
      isbn: null,
      subjects: main.subjects,
      shelves: main.related.flatMap((r) => {
        const shelf = catalogPath(r.href)
        return shelf
          ? [{ id: shelf, title: shelfTitle(r.title), description: null }]
          : []
      }),
      formats,
    }
  },

  async download(ctx, id, fid) {
    const entries = await builds(ctx, id)
    const known = entries.some((e) =>
      e.downloads.some((d) => formatId(id, d.href) === fid),
    )
    if (!known) throw new Error('Unknown format')
    return ctx.fetch(`${BASE}/ebooks/${id}.${fid}`)
  },
})
